# LLVM emitter gaps blocking std probes (document only)

File: oodac/docs/llvm_emit_gaps.oot

Status: SURVEY 2026-09-25. Grounded in serial `oodac build` runs of all
55 std probes with oodac 0.11.15 + oodar libs built from source + clang
22. 40 probes build; 15 fail at emit-llvm while `check` passes. Each
gap below is a check/emit divergence: the checker accepts code the
emitter cannot lower. No action taken: documenting only.

Reproduce: from the std repo root, with OODA_COMPILER pointing at
oodac/bin/oodac and jail dirs set to the workspace, run
`oodac build qa/<probe>.oo -o /tmp/x.bin` for any probe named below.

## Gap 1. Ok(Float) constructor — FIXED in source 2026-09-25

- Error: `ERR llvm Ok kind` (emit/llvm/ll_ctor.oo, end of ll_ctor_ok).
- Cause: no float branch and no %OoResF representation; worse,
  `Result[Float]` fell through the mapping into `resSt_Float`
  (a struct Result for a struct that cannot exist).
- Fix: new `resf` kind mirroring `resil` across 10 files:
  mapping + LLVM type + agg/mem predicates (ll_ty.oo),
  Ok/Err construction (ll_ctor.oo), match binding (ll_call.oo),
  val/err fields (ll_field.oo), unwrap gates + default kind
  (ll_method.oo), sret returns (ll_exit.oo), tag + err-string
  ARC with no payload call for the scalar (ll_arc.oo),
  `%OoResF = { i32, double, %OoStr }` preamble (ll_rt.oo),
  match-statement scrutinee gate incl. the missing `resol_`
  admit (ll_match.oo), and Result-typed struct field release
  (ll_struct_rr.oo). No runtime C change: scalars need no
  retain/release and the tag/err machinery is type-generic.
  Proven by a chain harness on the repro's real tokens
  (mapping + Ok + Err + sret return + match phi + unwrap +
  is_ok PASS), with a negative control on unfixed sources
  (maps to `resSt_Float`, FAIL).
- Shelf test: bootstrap/corpus/emit-llvm/pass/result_float_full.oo
  (expects `isok`/`m-ok`/`u-ok`; NOT wired into the CI gate
  until the fixed binary ships).
- Blocks: probe_science (via science/phys/classical/ideal_gas_law.oo).
  152 std files mention Result[Float; each needs an emit trial
  once the fixed binary ships.

## Gap 2. Net builtins unlowered — FIXED in source 2026-09-25

- Error: `ERR llvm unknown call tcp_connect` (emit/llvm/ll_user_call.oo).
- Cause: check knows tcp_connect/tcp_read/tcp_write (cap table), but
  no emitter dispatch lowers them. Runtime symbol oo_tcp_connect
  exists (liboodar-net.a). Same likely holds for the tcp_read,
  tcp_write, tcp_close, tcp_accept siblings.
- Fix: new emit/llvm/ll_builtin_net.oo with all five arms, sharing
  the sys OoResS helper (made pub); delegate hook in
  ll_builtin_host.oo; declare protos in ll_need_tab.oo; need
  registrations in ll_need.oo. Harness-proven with tcp gate.
- Shelf test: bootstrap/corpus/emit-llvm/pass/tcp_connect_refused.oo
  (prints `tcp-ok`; flipped to parity in the ledger 2026-09-28).
- Blocks: probe_cap_net.

## Gap 3. ord unlowered (call form and runtime) — FIXED in source 2026-09-25

- Error: `ERR llvm unknown call ord`.
- Cause: check lists `ord` as a known method name
  (check/tc_names_known.oo), but the emitter has no lowering and no
  oo_ord symbol exists in any oodar archive. Needs runtime + emit.
- Fix: new `long long oo_ord(OoStr s)` in oodar/core/str/str_ops.c
  (first byte via oo_byte_at, -1 when empty) + oodar.h declare;
  new arm in emit/llvm/ll_builtin.oo mirroring bytes_len (capless);
  declare proto + need registration. Harness-proven with negative
  control. Core lib rebuilt; symbol present.
- Shelf test: bootstrap/corpus/emit-llvm/pass/ord_first_byte.oo
  (expects `ord-ok`; NOT wired into the CI gate until the fixed
  binary ships).
- Blocks: probe_wayland_wire, probe_dbus_wire.

## Gap 4. Match arm type mismatch — FIXED in source 2026-09-25

- Error: `ERR llvm match arm type mismatch`.
- Cause: `Result[List[Struct]]` collapsed to kind `resl`
  (the string-list Result), so `Ok` built the wrong layout and
  the match bound the payload as `slist` while the default arm
  was `olist_X`. Minimal repro: match on `Result[List[Cell]]`
  with a `list_new()` default (m3b).
- Fix: new `resol_X` kind mirroring the `resSt_` idiom across
  8 files: mapping + LLVM type + agg/mem/ABI predicates
  (ll_ty.oo), `ll_is_resol` + wrapper type emission
  (ll_struct_list.oo), Ok/Err construction (ll_ctor.oo),
  match binding (ll_call.oo), val/err fields (ll_field.oo),
  unwrap gates (ll_method.oo), retain/release (ll_arc.oo), and
  import type emission (ll_struct_imp.oo). Representation:
  `%OoRes_OL_X = { i32, %OoL_X, %OoStr }`. Returns ride the
  generic sret tail via `ll_is_mem`; tag checks were already
  generic. Proven by a chain harness on the repro's real
  tokens (mapping + Ok + Err + match merge PASS), with a
  negative control on unfixed sources (maps to `resl`, FAIL).
  Note: `Result[List[Float]]` still maps to `resl` (same
  latent mistype, no probe hits it); fixing it needs a
  `%OoResFL` representation by the same recipe. Follow-up:
  struct fields typed `resol_X` skip retain/release in
  ll_struct_rr.oo (leak-only, no probe covers it).
- Shelf test: bootstrap/corpus/emit-llvm/pass/result_struct_list_match.oo
  (expects `1`; NOT wired into the CI gate until the fixed
  binary ships).
- Blocks: probe_data.

## Gap 5. dlopen/dlsym/dlclose mistyped as i64 — FIXED in source 2026-09-25

- Error: `ERR llvm method val kind i64` (field access `.val` on the
  dlopen result), or clang `invalid getelementptr indices` for
  is_err-only use.
- Cause: dlopen/dlsym/dlclose lower through the generic C-ABI guess,
  which yields kind i64. The runtime returns OoResS. Check treats
  the result as Result-like, so this is a check/emit kind divergence.
- Fix: explicit ext sig table (ll_ext_sig_ffi: dlopen/dlsym/dlclose
  to OoResS shapes) + sym mapping to oo_ forms; declare protos +
  need registrations. Harness-proven with negative control.
- Shelf test: bootstrap/corpus/emit-llvm/pass/dlopen_missing.oo
  (expects `dl-ok`; NOT wired into the CI gate until the fixed
  binary ships).
- Blocks: probe_sdl_window, probe_anim_2d, probe_sdl_blit, probe_sdl_gl.

## Gap 6. file_append_sync unlowered — FIXED in source 2026-09-25

- Error: `ERR llvm unknown call file_append_sync`.
- Cause: runtime symbol oo_file_append_sync exists
  (liboodar-core.a); no emitter dispatch maps the bare name.
- Fix: new dispatch arm in emit/llvm/ll_builtin_fs.oo using the
  resv3 helper (cap + path + content), mirroring fs_hardlink.
  Harness-proven: arm fires, emits the call plus fswrite gate;
  negative control on unfixed source fails as before.
- Shelf test: bootstrap/corpus/emit-llvm/pass/file_append_sync.oo
  (expects `fas-ok`; NOT wired into the CI gate until the fixed
  binary ships).
- Blocks: probe_wal_disk.

## Gap 7. Struct load without pointer — FIXED in source 2026-09-25

- Error: `ERR llvm struct load no ptr` (shipped binary); current
  source instead emitted an invalid empty-pointer field address.
- Cause: if/match expressions yield struct values with no home
  address; ll_struct_field_load ran the field address off the
  empty pointer. Minimal repro: `(if c { a } else { b }).id`.
- Fix: spill the struct value to a fresh temp in
  emit/llvm/ll_struct.oo, then address the field off the temp.
  Proven by a chain harness driving the new ll_expr/ll_ifexpr/
  ll_method sources on the repro's real tokens (PASS), with a
  negative control on unfixed sources (FAIL: empty-ptr GEP).
- Shelf test: bootstrap/corpus/emit-llvm/pass/struct_ifexpr_field.oo
  (expects `1`; NOT wired into the CI gate until the fixed
  binary ships).
- Blocks: probe_swarm.

## Gap 8. random unlowered — FIXED in source 2026-09-25

- Error: `ERR llvm unknown call random`.
- Fix: new arm in emit/llvm/ll_builtin_host.oo mirroring now_ms
  (i64, rand gate); declare proto + need registration.
  Harness-proven. Blocks: probe_cap_system.
- Shelf test: bootstrap/corpus/emit-llvm/pass/random_runs.oo
  (expects `rand-ok`; NOT wired into the CI gate until the fixed
  binary ships).

## Gap 9. landlock_restrict unlowered — FIXED in source 2026-09-25

- Error: `ERR llvm unknown call landlock_restrict`.
- Fix: new arm in emit/llvm/ll_builtin_sys.oo using the shared
  OoResS helper (cap + read dirs + write dirs); declare proto +
  need registration. Harness-proven with sys gate. Note: callers
  bind Result[Bool, String] but only use is_ok/is_err, which read
  the tag generically — the OoResS shape is sufficient.
- Shelf test: bootstrap/corpus/emit-llvm/pass/landlock_empty.oo
  (expects `ll-ok`; NOT wired into the CI gate until the fixed
  binary ships).
- Blocks: probe_sandbox_adv1, probe_sandbox_m1, probe_sandbox_stress.

## Notes for the fixer

- Parallel probe builds collide (shared .ooda-cache/tmp): one probe
  failed under xargs -P6 and passed serially. Measure serially.
- Emitter fixes cannot be verified without rebuilding oodac, and the
  self-host pipeline exceeds local build capacity (see the 360-minute
  CI job note in oodac/.github/workflows/ci.yml). Budget for that.
- The 15 failing probes are the regression suite: they already fail
  closed on every run. No new tests are needed to cover these gaps.
